 ials feeEase into summer with a day of watercolor inspired by Sonoma Count
 y’s sun-soaked abundance—ripe berries\, figs\, citrus\, fragrant herbs
 \, wild grasses\, and golden light stretching into the evening. Juicy reds
 \, warm yellows\, and deep greens set the mood for loose\, luminous painti
 ngs that feel relaxed\, ripe\, and deliciously seasonal.Focus on building 
 strong compositions using color\, texture\, light\, and form\, developed t
 hrough wet washes\, controlled washes\, and textural techniques. Guided di
 scussions explore the essential elements of visual art to help you create 
 expressive\, individual work.All materials provided\, Space limited to 10 
 studentsDiscussion break 12:30pm. Please bring a brown bag lunchAbout the 
