SUMMARY:Explore Gel Plate Printing — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, Ca
 lifornia
DTSTART:20260726T000000
DTEND:20260727T000000
UID:1a3fec34e4a8e69babb6cc5495cca9c8@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Explore Gel Plate Printing\, 7/26\n\n  \n    \n      \n       
  \n          $130.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSunday\, July 26\, 202
 6\; 11 AM – 3 PMFee: $115 + $15 materials feeAge: 16+ Learn to create be
 autiful designs on paper by printing with a gel plate and acrylic paint. M
 ixed media artist Catherine Cruz will teach you the basic skills for using
  this fun tool from printing textural backgrounds\, to layering colors\, a
 nd using stencils and other applications. You will take home many prints t
 hat can be used for designing collage\, mixed media art or greeting cards.
  This class is suitable for anyone wanting to learn this unique mono print
 ing style and perfect for beginners.What you’ll get from this workshop: 
 Methods for applying paint and pulling successful prints (Note: Magazine i
 mage transfer is not included in this class.)\, Techniques for creating in
 tricate layered designs\, Creative use of mark-making tools and masks\, St
 rategies for combining techniques.A variety of papers will be provided but
  you are highly encouraged to bring your own papers to experiment on.IMPOR
 TANT: Instructions for where to purchase your materials and how to prepare
  them is provided in the attached PDF. The instructor will start the class
  with a demonstration so please arrive a few minutes early to get set up s
 o we can start on time.  We will take a short break for lunch between 12:3
 0 and 1:00 pm so bring your lunch and a beverage.  About the instructor: C
 atherine Cruz is a French-American artist whose work is informed by textur
 es and patterns created by the passing of time and the effects of the natu
 ral elements on the built environment.  She holds a Bachelor of Science in
  interior design and she worked in the field of architectural design and g
 reen building certification for over 25 years.  She has taught collage and
  mixed media workshops in the Bay Area and in France since 2019\, and this
  is her fifth year at the Sebastopol Center for the Arts.  Her studio is l
 ocated in Sebastopol and she participates in Art Trails Open Studios.  You
  may contact Catherine at beyouartstudio@gmail.com.  Check out Catherine
 ’s other classes here:  https://wwws.sebarts.org/visual-arts-classes.\n\
